From 722e45da5782249ae96a541bc753abc54b78168a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:17:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(distro): recognize the vendor's apk-based distributions

Add the distro types VendorLinux and VendorHardened (for BellSoft: alpaquita
and bellsoft-hardened-containers), mapped from their /etc/os-release IDs.
Both carry ID_LIKE=alpine, so without the mapping they were treated as
Alpine and matched against the wrong feed. VERSION_ID is passed through
untouched (stream, 23, 25): "stream" is a rolling label that never reaches
end of life, the numbers are the LTS releases.

ParseDistroString handled only opensuse-leap as a hyphenated distro ID; it now
matches every hyphenated ID known to IDMapping (longest first), so that
--distro <hyphenated id>:stream and purl distro qualifiers parse.

Ported from the distro part of #3264.
---
